<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Diaspora.Modules.GeographicIntelligence</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Diaspora.Modules.GeographicIntelligence</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The Geographic Intelligence Platform (Phase B21). The backend behind the geographic half of
      the frontend's Phase 8 Maps and Navigation register — the neighbourhood score breakdown, the
      cost-of-living surface, the safety surface, the heat-map layer and the routing boundary.

      What this module owns: composing geographic intelligence out of facts other modules already
      hold, publishing the provenance around every figure it serves, and declaring the boundary an
      external geographic provider plugs into.

      What it deliberately does not own, and never duplicates:

        The places. B4 owns the catalogue — the hierarchy, the slugs, the centroids, the
        boundaries and the viewport search. This module resolves an area through B4 and adds
        nothing to it.

        The opinion about a place. B11 owns the neighbourhood profile — the liveability bands,
        their author, their approver and their review date. This module reads them through the
        published INeighborhoodDirectory and stores none of them.

        The counts. B4's ILocationResourceCounter registry has answered "how much of your vertical
        is in this node" since B4 shipped. The heat layer is that registry re-shaped, not a second
        count.

        Analytics is B19's. This module classifies geography; it aggregates nothing over time and
        records no event.

        Ranking is B14's, delivery is B13's, scheduling is B17's. A geographic condition is a fact
        this module can answer; what anybody does with it is theirs.

      It owns no table and ships no migration, which is the design rather than an omission: every
      figure it serves is composed at read time from a module that already holds it. A geographic
      intelligence layer with its own copy of a neighbourhood would be the duplication the whole
      phase brief forbids.

      Registers entirely through B2.6 contributor interfaces: no edit to the Platform Kernel, to
      Identity, or to Program.cs.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Two module references, both backwards, both to a published seam.

    Location composes at 300 and Housing at 1000; this module composes at 1900, so the module
    dependency guardrail — "a module never depends on a module composed after it" — permits both
    and the graph stays acyclic. The references buy exactly two things: B4's catalogue and counter
    registry, and B11's INeighborhoodDirectory. No aggregate, no repository and no identifier of
    either module is touched outside those seams.

    The alternative — consuming both through published integration events and keeping a third copy
    of every neighbourhood — is what Analytics does at 1800, and it is right for Analytics because
    analytics must record what was true at a moment. This module answers what is true now, so
    reading the owner directly is the correct shape and a projection would be a second truth that
    drifts.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions" />
    <!-- data.police.uk, for the safety counts. A named client, as Trust's decision publisher. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.SharedKernel\Diaspora.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Contracts\Diaspora.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Platform\Diaspora.Platform.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Application\Diaspora.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Location\Diaspora.Modules.Location.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Housing\Diaspora.Modules.Housing.csproj" />
    <!-- Corroborated community safety reports. Community is composed at 500, this module at 1900. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Diaspora.Modules.Community\Diaspora.Modules.Community.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
